    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was done:\n\n### Core Changes\n\n**frai-core (SDK)**:\n1. **index.js** - Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter and evaluate them\n2. **reporters.js** - Updated `toMarkdown()` to include a \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n3. **index.test.js** - Added 5 comprehensive tests covering threshold scenarios\n\n**frai-cli (CLI)**:\n1. **index.ts** - Added threshold parsing, validation, and exit code handling:\n   - `parseThresholds()` validates format and range (0-1)\n   - `getValidMetricIds()` lists available metrics for error messages\n   - `runEvalCommand()` integrates threshold evaluation with proper exit codes\n   - Updated eval command with `--threshold` option supporting multiple uses\n\n### Report Format\n\n**JSON** (when thresholds specified):\n- `passed`: boolean indicating if all thresholds passed\n- `thresholds`: array of `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries\n\n**Markdown** (when thresholds specified):\n- New \"Thresholds\" section showing `PASS`/`FAIL` for each threshold\n\n### Exit Codes\n- **0**: Success (all thresholds pass or none specified)\n- **1**: Threshold failure (report still written)\n- **2**: Usage error - malformed threshold, out-of-range minimum, or unknown metric (no report written)\n\n### Error Handling\n- Malformed thresholds show helpful error message\n- Unknown metrics list all valid metric IDs\n- Metrics with null/undefined scores fail their thresholds\n\n### Documentation\n- Updated both README files with CLI and SDK examples\n- Included valid metric IDs and usage patterns\n- Added complete SDK example showing threshold implementation\n\n### Backward Compatibility\n- Without `--threshold`, behavior is identical to before\n- All existing functionality preserved\n- New fields only appear in reports when thresholds are specified\n\nThe implementation is complete, tested, documented, and ready for use in CI pipelines to gate on evaluation metrics.",
